    "notes": "Native PMTiles footprints position the palace and the waterfront pavilions. Clearance probes pass through Gwanghwamun and the open south court gates at all levels. The short island bridge follows the original footway to the island. Exterior reconstruction of the principal palace courts, the island pavilion and the lake banquet hall. Additional service yards and outlying perimeter halls continue to use PMTiles. Carved animals, painted brackets and grilles are interpreted from photographs. Building datums follow the standard Terrarium samples. The lake and island use native map and terrain data. The island footbridge remains closed to public access in the source map."
  },
